%% Cost and latency are not the same axis. A cheaper model that needs more steps
%% is not cheaper. Measure cost per COMPLETED GOAL, never per API call.%%
%% bar  = small fast model   (cheap per call, needs more steps)
%% line = frontier reasoning (expensive per call, usually fewer steps)
%%
%% The crossover is the lesson: below ~6 steps the small model wins on cost,
%% above it the frontier model wins despite the higher unit price.
%% Numbers are illustrative, not benchmarks. Replace with your own measurements.
xychart-beta
    title "Illustrative cost per completed goal (USD)"
    x-axis ["1 step", "3 steps", "6 steps", "10 steps"]
    y-axis "USD per goal" 0 --> 0.60
    bar [0.02, 0.05, 0.09, 0.14]
    line [0.03, 0.11, 0.27, 0.52]